{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00288",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 5.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.54,
      "end_seconds": 12.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.32,
      "end_seconds": 20.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Well, um, so the thing is, I've got a mole that has changed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.28,
      "end_seconds": 24.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.35,
      "end_seconds": 39.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.66,
      "text": "About... well, about four days. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. And it bled once as well, you know, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.92,
      "end_seconds": 44.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.13,
      "end_seconds": 45.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.81,
      "end_seconds": 64.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any pain, history of skin cancer or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.75,
      "end_seconds": 67.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Um, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.08,
      "end_seconds": 71.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Right, your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.32,
      "end_seconds": 74.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Hmm, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.46,
      "end_seconds": 79.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.81,
      "end_seconds": 95.02,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 96.02,
      "end_seconds": 103.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Blood pressure 114 over 77, temperature is 36.8 degrees, heart rate 67, oxygen saturation is 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.44,
      "end_seconds": 116.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.42,
      "text": "Good, thank you. I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.69,
      "end_seconds": 119.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.26,
      "end_seconds": 124.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.33,
      "end_seconds": 128.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.19,
      "end_seconds": 131.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.63,
      "end_seconds": 133.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.54,
      "end_seconds": 151.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 164.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had epilepsy, yes. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.86,
      "end_seconds": 170.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Go on. Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.6,
      "end_seconds": 182.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Not at the moment, uh, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.93,
      "end_seconds": 184.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.95,
      "end_seconds": 187.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.49,
      "end_seconds": 203.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.4,
      "end_seconds": 207.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Thank you, um, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.43,
      "end_seconds": 211.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.42,
      "end_seconds": 213.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.4,
      "end_seconds": 226.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.8,
      "end_seconds": 230.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Okay, so that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.07,
      "end_seconds": 234.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.76,
      "end_seconds": 237.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.18,
      "end_seconds": 240.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.05,
      "end_seconds": 259.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I can't feel any glands in the armpit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.8,
      "end_seconds": 270.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Alright, I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.41,
      "end_seconds": 274.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Um, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.85,
      "end_seconds": 304.04,
      "duration_seconds": 29.19,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with a pigmented lesion that needs to be looked at more closely at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out a seborrhoeic keratosis yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a mole that has changed for about four days, and no pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.14,
      "end_seconds": 309.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.45,
      "end_seconds": 314.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.33,
      "end_seconds": 320.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Right, mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.31,
      "end_seconds": 345.66,
      "duration_seconds": 24.35,
      "text": "I'm going to order a skin biopsy, for changing mole. Please use sunscreen and cover up in the midday sun, and check your skin once a month. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll also refer you to a dermatologist. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Come back after the biopsy results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.74,
      "end_seconds": 354.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.97,
      "end_seconds": 360.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "So, I come back after the biopsy results. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.01,
      "end_seconds": 366.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, all right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.02,
      "end_seconds": 372.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.67,
      "end_seconds": 374.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}